  "major": "acting-bfa-nyc-9816b267",
  "major_name": "Acting",
  "degree": "BFA",
  "campus": "New York",
  "college": "College of Arts, Media and Design",
  "overview_text": "The Bachelor of Fine Arts in Acting program is designed to develop the skills and techniques required for a successful career in performance. It aims to provide students with a comprehensive education in acting, encompassing both classical and contemporary approaches, while fostering creativity, discipline, and professional readiness. The program is committed to preparing students for diverse opportunities in theater, film, television, and other performance-based mediums. The program emphasizes hands-on experience, with numerous performance opportunities and collaborations with experienced faculty and industry professionals. The program is intended for students with a passion for performance and a desire to pursue a professional acting career; who are interested in exploring the full spectrum of acting from stage to screen; and who seek a structured, immersive education in the craft.",
  "source_text": "Complete all courses listed below unless otherwise indicated. Also complete any corequisite labs, recitations, clinicals, or tools courses where specified and complete any additional courses needed beyond specific college and major requirements to satisfy graduation credit requirements.\nUniversitywide Requirements\nAll undergraduate students are required to complete the\nUniversitywide Requirements\n.\nNUpath Requirements\nAll undergraduate students are required to complete the\nNUpath Requirements\n.\nNew York State Liberal Arts and Sciences Requirements\nAll undergraduate students enrolled in programs at the New York campus are required to fulfill\nNew York State Liberal Arts and Sciences requirements\n.\nMajor Required Courses\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nTHTR 1111\nStagecraft\n4\nTHTR 2020\nVoice and Speech for the Actor 1\n4\nTHTR 2040\nVoice and Speech for the Actor 2\n4\nTHTR 2110\nActing: Process and Technique\n4\nTHTR 2120\nBeginning Scene Study\n4\nTHTR 2150\nScript Analysis\n4\nTHTR 2240\nMovement for Actors 1\n4\nTHTR 2241\nMovement for Actors 2\n4\nTHTR 2450\nTheatre Histories 1: Early Evidence Through 1750\n4\nTHTR 2455\nTheatre Histories 2: 1750 Through Tomorrow\n4\nTHTR 3050\nElements of Directing\n4\nTHTR 3110\nShakespeare, the Stage, and Humanity\n4\nTHTR 4060\nActing: Heightened Language and Historical Contexts\n4\nTHTR 4140\nActing: Shakespeare\n4\nTHTR 4410\nActing: Intermediate Scene Study\n4\nTHTR 4420\nActing: Advanced Scene Study\n4\nTHTR 4650\nAdvanced Studies in Drama and Theatre\n4\nComplete the following course twice, studying different topics in each term:\n8\nTHTR 4973\nSpecial Topics in Acting\nComplete one dramatic literature course (ENGL or THTR)\n4\nGeneral Electives/NUpath\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nComplete any remaining semester hours after major to fulfill NUpath courses and to reach the minimum semester-hour program requirement.\nActing\nMajor Credit Requirement\nComplete 80 semester hours in the major.\nProgram Requirement\n128 total semester hours required",
